KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the init-capture moved: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ the capture copied: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The closure's member of class type is direct-initialized by its move
constructor from the init-capture's xvalue, and by its copy constructor
for a capture by copy.  CBMC declared the init-capture's member as a
reference (the type of `static_cast<M &&>(m)') and initialized members
without constructors: neither counter changed.  C++17 makes the copy of
the closure into f and g a guaranteed elision, so each counter changes
once.
